                <pb facs="0740" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363 Barco/122: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Piles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-30T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1928—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Department’s 40, July 27, 6 p.m. Delivered note to Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs today. He expressed approval of its contents. Impossible to see
                    President today but hope to have interview tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Piles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
